// Multi-limb trial division: N held as little-endian 64-bit limbs, so there is
// no 64-bit size cap on the input. Trial division needs only N mod d for a
// small candidate d, and N mod d is a Horner fold over the limbs from the top
// down, each step ((r<<64)|limb) % d carried in a 128-bit intermediate. The
// candidate d itself stays a u64, so the __int128 modulo is exact. The square
// root of a large N is unreachable, so the sweep is bounded by a divisor
// ceiling dceil instead of d*d<=N: this finds every prime factor of N below
// dceil, of an N of any width, and reports none within the ceiling otherwise.
